{"title":"2002 OIM Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A police officer tries to catch a thief on a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa57403610de7494d3437211af9fb81057351a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001 \\times 2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> board. They play alternately. Each player, on his turn, must move one square in one of the three senses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d95bdb4067e8005d19d15bfbd4e83d8980336c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\downarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"9\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea4e52bb41fa9c0a1f8a387ea39b5b9c993b74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\to$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e399241c1cd2d58d0a397fd94728a5d6f60022d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nwarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>If the policeman is in the bottom right corner square, he can use his turn to move directly to the square in the upper left corner (the thief cannot do this move).\n</p><p>Initially the policeman is in the central square and the thief is in the neighboring diagonal square top right to the policeman. The policeman starts the game. Show that:\n</p><p>1. The thief manages to move at least 10,000 without being caught.\n</p><p>2. The police officer has a strategy to capture the thief.\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> The policeman captures the thief when he enters the square where the thief is. If the thief enters the police officer's box, there is no capture.\n</p><p>~translated into English by Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2002_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_OIM_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe18.htm\">https://www.oma.org.ar/enunciados/ibe18.htm</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201133\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 36/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 423/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 715/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.397      1 Template:Solution\n100.00%    5.397      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26138:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017201133 and revision id 207251. Rendering wa